<<<
depend. The slovenly construction illustrated below, in which it depends is followed by an indirect question without upon, is growing common, but is indefensible:— Critics ought to be artists who have failed’. Ought they? It all depends who is going to read the criticism, & what he expects to learn from it. dependable. For such formations
===
**depend.** The slovenly construction illustrated below, in which *it depends* is followed by an indirect question without *upon*, is growing common, but is indefensible:—'*Critics ought to be artists who have failed*'. Ought they? *It all depends who is going to read the criticism, & what he expects to learn from it.*

**dependable.** For such formations
>>>
